+## CR-UI: a calmer, clearer creator list (2026-11-15)
+
+Owner decision "TALK QUESTS AND A CLEANER, PRETTIER UI" item 2, first step. What changed (pixels move on the list and the
+grid footer only; the panels, tabs, pane and pickers are as before):
+
+* **The footer is the description line.** It names the cursor's value in full. When "name n/N - set" is too wide it drops the
+  set, then the count, and only a name that is still too wide scrolls (`footer_text`, `name_tail`). Before, the GBA cut the
+  name ("tars..", "Heavy Dr..") and scrolled the row.
+* **Calm motion.** The selected row of a part, list or colour value is cut with ".." and stands still (`footer_names`); only
+  the preset rows (their footer says "browse / apply") still scroll. The picture grid's footer shows the name alone when the
+  set does not fit, so it does not scroll either. `value_moves` / `footer_moves` / `grid_footer_moves` say so to the retained
+  panel keys (S3-3's recipe is kept: a still list is put back from the last frame).
+* **Fewer captions.** No caption repeats the tab's name: the Hair tab lost "Hair" (one more row on the GBA), the Voice tab's
+  second caption is "Tuning", the Body tab's is "Shape" (the title reads "Body > Shape").
+* **The sliders page says the cheat.** A build slider's line shows "Short <-> Tall  x3" while Slider range is above x1.
+* **Room for CR-PERS.** A test pins that the tab strip has room for a tenth page on 240x160.
+
+Tests (`test_creator.c`): `cr_ui_footer_names_every_value` (every part / list / colour choice: the footer has the whole name,
+the row does not scroll), `cr_ui_tab_strip_has_room_for_one_more_page`, `cr_ui_no_caption_repeats_the_tab`,
+`cr_ui_slider_line_names_the_range`. Before / after shots at 240x160 and 320x240 (creator, creator_sliders, creator_grid)
+and contact sheets were kept with the evidence.
